    "question": {
      "text": "The subtraction of a binary number $B$ from another binary number $A$, done by adding the 2’s complement of $B$ to $A$, results in a binary number without carry, this implies that the result is:",
      "type": "MCQ",
      "options": [
        {
          "label": "A",
          "text": "negative and is in normal form"
        },
        {
          "label": "B",
          "text": "positive and is in normal form"
        },
        {
          "label": "C",
          "text": "negative and is in 2’s complement form"
        },
        {
          "label": "D",
          "text": "positive and is in 2’s complement form"
        }
      ],
      "marks": null,
      "negativeMarks": null,
      "difficulty": null
    },
    "answer": {
      "correctOption": "C",
      "correctText": "negative and is in 2’s complement form",
      "explanation": "$A-B$ has to be performed. The 2’s complement of $B$ (which is $2^n-B$, $n=$ number of bits in $B$) is added to $A$.\n\nSo result is $A+2^n-B$, and there is no carry:\n$A+2^n-B=2^n-(A-B)$.\n\nSo, the result is negative and it is in 2’s complement form.\nChoice (C).",
      "status": "confirmed"
    },
    "classification": {
      "subject": "Digital Logic",
      "topic": "Digital Logic",
      "subtopic": null,
      "tags": []
    },
