    "question": {
      "text": "Parity is a common error detection mechanism that is often used in data reception or retrieval systems. Consider a parity encoder that is used for data transmission or storage. If a word contains an even number of 1’s, the parity bit is 0. If the word has odd number of 1’s the parity bit is 1. If the data is $w,x,y,z$ then the min terms for parity bit is?",
