      "correctText": "4",
      "explanation": "Convert to decimal number system:\n$$\\frac{3r^2+0r+2}{2r+0}=r+2+\\frac1r.$$\nAlso,\n$$12.1_r=r+2+\\frac1r.$$\nHence\n$$\\frac{3r^2+2}{2r}=r+2+\\frac1r.$$\nSo $3r^2+2=2r^2+4r+2$, giving $r^2=4r$ and $r=0$ or $4$. The valid base is $r=4$.\nChoice (C).",
